// Harness self-test fixture (PRD section 7) -- NOT a real builtin.
//
// The leading underscore in the filename marks this as a meta-fixture
// for the conformance harness itself, not a per-builtin conformance
// pair. Its only purpose is to keep test_harness_discovers_at_least_smoke_pair
// green so a future commit that breaks the auto-discovery glob
// cannot silently turn the entire conformance suite into "no tests
// collected" (which CI would happily pass).
//
// Body is deliberately minimal: a 2-bar SMA(1) which is just the
// close itself. When the compiler lands the pair will start
// asserting the trivial identity close == sma; until then the
// conformance test SKIPs for this pair (no compiler) but the
// harness self-test still validates that discovery picked it up.
//@version=6
indicator("smoke", overlay=true)
plot(ta.sma(close, 1), title="sma_close")
